 \subsection{What detailed balance removes: circulation flows}\label{sec:circulation}
-For a stationary distribution $\pi$ and transition matrix $P$, the net probability flow from $i$ to $j$ is $J_{ij}=\pi_iP_{ij}-\pi_jP_{ji}$. Stationarity makes the three independent entries equal, $J_{12}=J_{23}=J_{31}=j_t$, so one scalar measures the mass rotating around the state cycle at each origin. Detailed balance is $j_t=0$, which the reversible parameterization imposes by construction. Because terciles are equal-count cutpoints, the fitted stationary distribution stays within $4\times10^{-4}$ of uniform at every origin, and $j_t$ is then approximately one third of the corresponding pairwise difference in transition probabilities.
